  "unit": "Unit 14 - Quadratics",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 14 - Quadratics for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 14 - Quadratics — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 14 - Quadratics for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n<p>The <strong>roots/solutions</strong> of a quadratic are the <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>-values where <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n<strong>Methods</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Factoring</strong><br/>\n   Example: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> </li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><strong>Quadratic Formula</strong><br/>\n   For <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>:  </li>\n</ol>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>±</mi><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Completing the Square</strong> (see below).  </li>\n</ol>\n<hr />\n<p>Transform quadratic into vertex form.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> by completing the square.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Set <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>±</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>So <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n<p>1) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.\n2) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> using quadratic formula.\n3) Find vertex of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.\n<p>A parabola’s vertex is given by:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mspace width=\"negativethinmathspace\"></mspace><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>\n<p>Vertex form:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math>\n<p>where <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math> = vertex.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong> </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>Vertex: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><br/>\nVertex = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<hr />\n<p>The discriminant is inside quadratic formula:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> → 2 real roots  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> → 1 real root (double root)  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> → no real roots (complex roots)  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong> </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math></p>\n<p>→ no real solutions.  </p>\n<hr />\n<p>Quadratics model motion, area, profit, etc.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br />Height of ball: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow></math> (feet).</p><ul><li>Vertex gives maximum height.</li></ul>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><br/>\nMax height = 64 ft at <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> sec.  </p>\n<hr />\n<ul>\n<li>Always check if factoring is quick.  </li>\n<li>Memorize quadratic formula.  </li>\n<li>Discriminant saves time for “how many solutions” questions.  </li>\n<li>Parabolas open upward if <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, downward if <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>1) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n2) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> using quadratic formula<br/>\n3) Find vertex of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n4) Determine number of real roots of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n5) A ball’s height is <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></math>. Find maximum height.  </p>\n<hr />\n<p>1) Factor: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>:  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>±</mi><msqrt><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>±</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>49</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>±</mi><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>\n<p>3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>. Vertex <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>4) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> → no real roots.  </p>\n<p>5) Vertex: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><br/>\nMax height = 50.  </p>\n<p><strong>More practice</strong></p>\n<p>Keep going—aim for accuracy first, then speed.</p>\n<p><strong>Mixed practice set</strong></p>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n4) Determine number of real roots of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.\n5) A ball’s height is <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow></math>. Find maximum height.",
